# client-report-generator — credential & config checklist
#
# This workflow needs NO environment variables: every secret attaches to
# a node as an n8n credential, so it runs unchanged on n8n Cloud and
# self-hosted instances. There is nothing to copy to .env — use this
# file as the checklist of what to create under n8n → Credentials and
# attach on each node. Full walkthrough: SETUP.md.
# Quick demo: press "Test workflow" — zero credentials needed.
#
# ── n8n credentials to create ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Google Sheets — credential type: Google Sheets OAuth2
#    nodes: Read config tab · Read reports ledger · Record report ·
#           Create report workbook · Write config tab · Write reports tab
#
# 2. Gmail — credential type: Gmail OAuth2
#    nodes: Send report email · Create report draft ·
#           Email operator: run digest · Email owner: workflow error
#
# 3. OpenAI — credential type: OpenAI API key
#    node:  Write report narrative (AI)   (model pinned: gpt-4o-mini)
#
# 4. Meta Ads — credential type: Header Auth
#    (genericCredentialType: httpHeaderAuth)
#    node:   Fetch Meta Ads insights
#    header: Authorization = Bearer <Meta Marketing API access token>
#
# 5. Google Ads — credential type: Custom Auth
#    (genericCredentialType: httpCustomAuth)
#    node:   Fetch Google Ads metrics
#    TWO headers ride in one credential JSON — both are required:
#      Authorization    = Bearer <Google Ads OAuth access token>
#      developer-token  = <Google Ads developer token>
#
# 6. GA4 — credential type: Header Auth
#    (genericCredentialType: httpHeaderAuth)
#    node:   Fetch GA4 report
#    header: Authorization = Bearer <Google Analytics Data API token>
#
# 7. Slack — credential type: Header Auth
#    (genericCredentialType: httpHeaderAuth)
#    node:   Post report to Slack
#    header: Authorization = Bearer <Slack bot token, chat:write scope>
#
# ── node-level placeholders to edit (not env vars) ─────────────────────
#
#   Workflow Config node → sheet_id = PASTE_SPREADSHEET_ID_HERE
#     (the SETUP lane prints it; or any workbook with config + reports tabs)
#   Operator email node  → to       = owner@example.com
#     (receives the failure alerts AND the weekly run digest)
#   config tab rows      → per client: src_meta_ads / src_google_ads /
#     src_ga4 / sink_gmail / sink_slack flags, recipients_email /
#     slack_channel, meta_ad_account_id / google_ads_customer_id /
#     ga4_property_id, and optional delivery_mode, brand_name /
#     brand_color / brand_logo_url, alert_threshold_pct cells
#
# ── live vs demo ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   No disabled nodes and no env switch — the demo lane is structural.
#   The four fixture rows emitted by "Demo config (fixture)" carry
#   live:false, and the gating IFs (… live? gates + delivery_mode
#   routing) steer them to demo adapters and demo sinks, so a demo run
#   never reaches a credential node. Rows read from the real config tab
#   default to live → real fetches and sends.
#
#   Optional: Settings → Error workflow → pick this same workflow to arm
#   the "On workflow error" lane — it is inert until wired (see the
#   Reliability section of README.md).
